# S17 ("the wise are the learners and not the unlearned") borrows the sense of "learn" from the dictation case of S15–S16. There, learning means following or understanding what is said. S11/S13 meant gaining knowledge one lacked.
# Likewise, "unlearned" in S17 is set against "wise" as clever pupils, so it means slow pupils, not ignorant ones.
# No premise or assumption joins the two senses. The shift happens in the conclusion's denial of S13, so I name no bridge.
